Philippe the horse (or I guess you can

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:44.319
consider the Beast himself). Cinderella?
Dress and her mice Jaq and Gus. Snow

00:12:44.319 --> 00:12:46.660
White and Sleeping Beauty? Sresses and
general

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:51.220
woodland creatures. Merida? Dress and
Angus the horse, and now let's look at

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:55.629
that excluded list. Meg from Hercules? No
animal. Princess Eilonwy from Black

00:12:55.629 --> 00:12:59.620
Cauldron? No animal. Esmerelda from
Hunchback? OK she's got herself a

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:03.189
dress and a goat, but she's also an outlaw
who's treated as an object of sexual

00:13:03.189 --> 00:13:06.850
desire by the men in the movie soooo she's
got a couple other things working

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:10.750
against her in this qualification. Anna
Elsa? Sure they have Olaf, but he's

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:14.529
technically not an animal and honestly
they do make the cut when it comes to a

00:13:14.529 --> 00:13:18.670
separate list of Disneyland theme park
princesses, in which they're the only new

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:22.839
additions. Quite frankly animal plus
dress is the only set of qualifications

00:13:22.839 --> 00:13:27.610
that clearly delineates the princesses
from the not princesses. But that still

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:31.509
leaves out Moana. What about her? She
clearly has Heihei the rooster so

00:13:31.509 --> 00:13:35.290
what's holding her back? It's the dress.
Despite what Maui might call her

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:39.399
outfit, first off it's technically not
addressed by dictionary definition which

00:13:39.399 --> 00:13:42.639
is a one-piece garment for a woman or
girl that covers the body and extends

00:13:42.639 --> 00:13:45.699
down to the legs. However, Jasmine from Aladdin also

00:13:45.699 --> 00:13:48.579
doesn't wear a traditional dress for
most of her movie so that's not the main

00:13:48.579 --> 00:13:53.769
problem going on here. What is the issue
is what Moana's dress represents. Consider

00:13:53.769 --> 00:13:57.250
this according to an interview with the
site Tyranny of Style, Neysa Bové,

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:01.389
visual development artist and key costume
designer for Moana, emphasizes the goal

00:14:01.389 --> 00:14:05.319
of staying true to Pacific Islander
culture, quote, "The biggest challenge on

00:14:05.319 --> 00:14:10.029
the film was the limited materials. We
only had two, 'tapa' and 'pandanus.' Tapa is

00:14:10.029 --> 00:14:12.880
made from the mulberry tree bark. They
pull out the bark and go through a

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:16.120
strenuous process of making a paste and
eventually tap it all together

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:20.259
hence 'tapa.' Similar story with the
pandanus weaving. Pandanus is actually a

00:14:20.259 --> 00:14:24.220
tree and they pull the pandanus leaves
and shred them into strips. These dry and

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:27.819
later you take each piece and weave it
together. You can even braid it! We had a

00:14:27.819 --> 00:14:32.319
specific rule, if you can find it in the
island, you can make it." end quote. Staying

00:14:32.319 --> 00:14:35.680
true to the materials, history and
culture of the Pacific Islands was

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:39.309
essential for this movie and its
characters. Now look at the eleven

00:14:39.309 --> 00:14:43.180
existing princesses. Each and every one
wearing pretty generic attire that

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:47.949
alludes to their culture of origin
vaguely at best. Times are different now

00:14:47.949 --> 00:14:51.550
and Disney is under more scrutiny than
ever about its appropriation of other

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:56.050
cultures for money. It's an issue that
hung over the head of Moana from before

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:59.980
the movie's release and
continues to do so today, with specific

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:04.000
focus on the costumes. And if the goal of
all the Disney Princesses is to have

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:07.899
young girls wear your dress and look
like the character, Moana's outfit, while

00:15:07.899 --> 00:15:11.290
terrifically designed and culturally
sensitive from a movie standpoint,

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:14.980
becomes really problematic when you
start churning out cheap copies to sell

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:19.089
next to your malls Sunglass Huts. So what
makes a princess? Well according to

00:15:19.089 --> 00:15:22.720
Disney it's not who you are, what you do
or even who you choose to marry. It's

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:28.000
what you wear that counts, and isn't that
the best message to send to little girls.

